    {
      "id": "hacks-five-parking",
      "scene": "离开办公室前，前台询问是否需要停车优惠验证。",
      "purpose": "询问需要 → 确认 → 告知要等一下并找人帮忙。",
      "hints": [
        {
          "expression": "Do you need…?",
          "meaning": "你需要……吗？"
        },
        {
          "expression": "That’s gonna take me a minute.",
          "meaning": "我需要一点时间。"
        }
      ],
      "turns": [
        {
          "speaker": "前台",
          "text": "Girly, do you need validation?",
          "translation": "姑娘，你需要停车优惠验证吗？"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "访客",
          "text": "Yeah.",
          "translation": "需要。"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "前台",
          "text": "Oh, God. Crap, girl. That’s gonna take me a minute. Bill, can you get Kelly to help me?",
          "translation": "哎呀，糟了，姑娘，这得花我一点时间。Bill，你能叫 Kelly 来帮我吗？"
        }
      ],
      "notes": "gonna 是 going to 的口语形式。take me a minute 常表示需要一点时间，不一定恰好一分钟。girly/girl 很随意；crap 是轻度粗口，无需照搬。",
